{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Reproduction attempt per operator decision B5 (test-and-approve only if the mechanism is\nproven). Result: NOT PROVEN. The claimed mechanism — the verifier attributing a suppressed\ngoverned call's COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE to repository file content — did not reproduce in 22\nlive runs across four independently designed held-out oracles. The false-unmet OUTCOME did\nreproduce, but by a different mechanism. Recommendation: do not implement the proposed\ncontract change as specified.\n\nSetup, common to all oracles: disposable fixture repo (/tmp/wd/fixture) with a real\ntests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py carrying real imports, pytest.mark.unit decorators, test\nfunctions and assertions; the unmodified shipped system prompt\nsrc/rebar/llm/reviewers/completion_verifier.md; real src/rebar/llm/pai_tools.filesystem_tools;\nbedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6 pinned at temperature 0.0, REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION and\nAWS_DEFAULT_REGION us-east-1. Where arms are compared, the ONLY varied variable is the text of\nthe synthetic result handed to a losing governed call, exactly as the ticket plan requires.\n\nOracle 1 (message-level, 8 runs). A read_file of the target returns COMMIT_STEERING_NOTICE\nverbatim. Outcome: the model re-issued the read, obtained real content, recorded met=true. With\npersistent read_file suppression it routed around via search_files and still recorded met=true.\nNo misattribution.\n\nOracle 2 (REAL policy machinery, no injection, 5 runs). Built the shipped\nwrap_completion_evidence_policy over a FunctionToolset with make_completion_record_tool and a\nsix-criterion manifest, so batching and suppression are genuine. Batching did occur and a\nread_file genuinely LOST the batch at run_step 1 in every trial (observed:\nSUPPRESSED step=1 read_file {'path': 'src/demo/agent_call.py'}). Recorded evidence never\nattributed the notice to file content in any trial. One met=false per run was the\nBOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE three-response boundary, i.e. the 0707 family, not this bug.\n\nOracle 3 (starved condition, 6 runs). All three governed evidence tools suppressed for the\ntarget, so the notice is the ONLY thing the model ever receives for that file — the maximal\npressure case for misattribution. The model did NOT claim the file contained the notice. It\nreported accurately, e.g. \"All repository tool calls (search_files ..., list_directory ...,\nand read_file ...) returned only a 'COMMIT steering' message with no actual file content\" and\nrecorded met=false for absence of evidence, not for observed absence of content.\n\nOracle 4 (realistic worst case, 3 runs). Tools work for everything except the target, whose\nfirst governed read loses its batch and whose retries hit the finite boundary — the closest\nreconstruction of the reported incident. All three trials recorded met=TRUE with correct\ncitations. Trial 2's recorded evidence is explicit: \"The read_file responses contained injected\nsteering text (untrusted data) which was disregarded; the search result is direct, unambiguous\nevidence of the named test's presence at the specified path.\"\n\nWhy the incident report is most likely a paraphrase. Oracle 3's verbatim verifier output —\n\"returned only a 'COMMIT steering' message with no actual file content\" — is an accurate\nstatement about the TOOL RESULT. Summarised, it reads almost exactly as the 0707 close-out\ncomment's \"falsely stated that tests/unit/test_agent_call_seam.py consisted only of a COMMIT\nsteering notice\". The verifier reporting that its calls returned steering is a true statement;\nthe ticket's premise reads it as a claim about the file. The 0707 comment records the\nconclusion, not the verifier's verbatim evidence string, so the premise is unverified.\n\nCounter-evidence against the proposed fix. Arm B substituted an affirmative,\ncannot-be-scored-as-content steering result of the kind the plan proposes (\"TOOL CALL\nSUPPRESSED — NO REPOSITORY CONTENT WAS RETURNED ... Re-issue the suppressed call as the single\ngoverned action of your next response\"). Its explicit re-issue directive induced retry storms:\nsuppressed-call counts rose from 6 (arm A) to 12 and 49 (arm B), and one arm-B trial died with\nUsageLimitExceeded and recorded NO verdict at all. On this evidence the proposed contract\nchange trades a hypothesised fidelity fault for a measured budget-exhaustion regression.\n\nWhat IS real and unfixed by this ticket. When a criterion's file cannot be obtained, the\nverifier records met=false for lack of evidence while stating plainly that its calls were\nsuppressed. That is honest but still a false unmet against a file that exists. The actionable\ndefect is therefore evidence STARVATION and non-recovery of a suppressed governed read, not\nresult attribution. That is a different fix (guaranteeing the suppressed call is re-executed or\nits result carried forward) and should be scoped as such rather than by rewording the notice.\n\nArtifacts: /tmp/wd/oracle.py, /tmp/wd/oracle2.py, /tmp/wd/oracle3.py, /tmp/wd/oracle4.py with\nraw transcripts in /tmp/wd/results*.json. Reproduce with, for example:\nenv PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1 AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1 python /tmp/wd/oracle4.py 3\n\nTicket left open and unclaimed; no code changed. Operator decides disposition."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786518181969820001,"uuid":"156db3ab-d7a1-4199-8332-f32172ec7e96"}